From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Liao <wcliaw610@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:54:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kitty): place unicode placeholders in the right column

write_placeholder() moved the cursor to column x, but x is 0-based, as
y is (which it already adds 1 to), so every placeholder image was drawn
one column left of where it was meant to be. The normal kitty method
moves to x + 1.
---
 lua/image/backends/kitty/helpers.lua | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lua/image/backends/kitty/helpers.lua b/lua/image/backends/kitty/helpers.lua
index cd20a74..0133c22 100644
--- a/lua/image/backends/kitty/helpers.lua
+++ b/lua/image/backends/kitty/helpers.lua
@@ -124,7 +124,8 @@ local write_placeholder = function(image_id, x, y, width, height)
 
   write(foreground)
   for i = 0, height - 1 do
-    move_cursor(x, y + i + 1)
+    -- x is 0-based, like y; the terminal's columns start at 1
+    move_cursor(x + 1, y + i + 1)
     for j = 0, width - 1 do
       write(codes.placeholder .. codes.diacritics[i + 1] .. codes.diacritics[j + 1])
     end
